{
  "title": "32: al-Sajdah السجدة",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nالٓمّٓ‏(1)\n\nAlif, Lam, Meem.\nۚ تَنْزِيْلُ الْكِتٰبِ لَا رَيْبَ فِيْهِ مِنْ رَّبِّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَؕ‏(2)\n\nThe [gradual] sending down of the Book, there is no doubt in it, is from the Lord of all the worlds.\nاَمْ يَقُوْلُوْنَ افْتَرٰٮهُ‌ۚ بَلْ هُوَ الْحَقُّ مِنْ رَّبِّكَ لِتُنْذِرَ قَوْمًا مَّاۤ اَتٰٮهُمْ مِّنْ نَّذِيْرٍ مِّنْ قَبْلِكَ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَهْتَدُوْنَ‏(3)\n\nBut they say, ‘He has fabricated it.’ No, it is the truth from your Lord, that you may warn a people to whom there did not come any warner before you, so that they may be guided [to the right path].\nاَللّٰهُ الَّذِىْ خَلَقَ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضَ وَمَا بَيْنَهُمَا فِىْ سِتَّةِ اَيَّامٍ ثُمَّ اسْتَوٰى عَلَى الْعَرْشِ‌ؕ مَا لَكُمْ مِّنْ دُوْنِهٖ مِنْ وَّلِىٍّ وَّلَا شَفِيْعٍ‌ؕ اَفَلَا تَتَذَكَّرُوْنَ‏(4)\n\nIt is Allah who created the heavens and the earth and whatever is between them in six days, then He settled on the Throne. You do not have besides Him any guardian or intercessor. Will you not then take admonition?\nيُدَبِّرُ الْاَمْرَ مِنَ السَّمَآءِ اِلَى الْاَرْضِ ثُمَّ يَعْرُجُ اِلَيْهِ فِىْ يَوْمٍ كَانَ مِقْدَارُهٗۤ اَلْفَ سَنَةٍ مِّمَّا تَعُدُّوْنَ‏(5)\n\nHe directs the command from the heaven to the earth; then it ascends toward Him in a day whose span is a thousand years by your reckoning.\nذٰلِكَ عٰلِمُ الْغَيْبِ وَالشَّهَادَةِ الْعَزِيْزُ الرَّحِيْمُۙ‏(6)\n\nThat is the Knower of the sensible and the Unseen, the All-mighty, the All-merciful,\nالَّذِىْۤ اَحْسَنَ كُلَّ شَىْءٍ خَلَقَهٗ‌ وَبَدَاَ خَلْقَ الْاِنْسَانِ مِنْ طِيْنٍ‌ۚ‏(7)\n\nwho perfected everything that He created and commenced man’s creation from clay.\nثُمَّ جَعَلَ نَسْلَهٗ مِنْ سُلٰلَةٍ مِّنْ مَّآءٍ مَّهِيْنٍ‌ۚ‏(8)\n\nThen He made his progeny from an extract of a base fluid.\nثُمَّ سَوّٰٮهُ وَنَفَخَ فِيْهِ مِنْ رُّوْحِهٖ‌ وَجَعَلَ لَكُمُ السَّمْعَ وَالْاَبْصَارَ وَالْاَفْئِدَةَ ‌ ؕ قَلِيْلًا مَّا تَشْكُرُوْنَ‏(9)\n\nThen He proportioned him and breathed into him of His Spirit, and made for you hearing, sight, and hearts. Little do you thank.\nوَقَالُوْٓا ءَاِذَا ضَلَلْنَا فِى الْاَرْضِ ءَاِنَّا لَفِىْ خَلْقٍ جَدِيْدٍ ؕ ‌بَلْ هُمْ بِلِقَآءِ رَبِّهِمْ كٰفِرُوْنَ‏(10)\n\nThey say, ‘When we have been lost in the dust, shall we be indeed created anew?’ Indeed, they disbelieve in the encounter with their Lord.\nقُلْ يَتَوَفّٰٮكُمْ مَّلَكُ الْمَوْتِ الَّذِىْ وُكِّلَ بِكُمْ ثُمَّ اِلٰى رَبِّكُمْ تُرْجَعُوْنَ‏(11)\n\nSay, ‘You will be taken away by the angel of death, who has been charged with you. Then you will be brought back to your Lord.’\nوَلَوْ تَرٰٓى اِذِ الْمُجْرِمُوْنَ نَاكِسُوْا رُءُوْسِهِمْ عِنْدَ رَبِّهِمْ رَبَّنَاۤ اَبْصَرْنَا وَسَمِعْنَا فَارْجِعْنَا نَعْمَلْ صَالِحًا اِنَّا مُوْقِنُوْنَ‏(12)\n\nWere you to see when the guilty hang their heads before their Lord [confessing], ‘Our Lord! We have seen and heard. Send us back so that we may act righteously. Indeed we are [now] convinced.’\nوَ لَوْ شِئْنَا لَاٰتَيْنَا كُلَّ نَفْسٍ هُدٰٮهَا وَلٰكِنْ حَقَّ الْقَوْلُ مِنِّىْ لَاَمْلَئَنَّ جَهَنَّمَ مِنَ الْجِنَّةِ وَالنَّاسِ اَجْمَعِيْنَ‏(13)\n\nHad We wished We would have given every soul its guidance, but My word became due [against the faithless]: ‘Surely I will fill hell with all the [guilty] jinn and humans.’\nفَذُوْقُوْا بِمَا نَسِيْتُمْ لِقَآءَ يَوْمِكُمْ هٰذَا‌ ۚ اِنَّا نَسِيْنٰكُمْ‌ وَذُوْقُوْا عَذَابَ الْخُلْدِ بِمَا كُنْتُمْ تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(14)\n\nSo taste [the punishment] for your having forgotten the encounter of this day of yours. We [too] have forgotten you. Taste the everlasting punishment because of what you used to do.\nاِنَّمَا يُؤْمِنُ بِاٰيٰتِنَا الَّذِيْنَ اِذَا ذُكِّرُوْا بِهَا خَرُّوْا سُجَّدًا وَّسَبَّحُوْا بِحَمْدِ رَبِّهِمْ وَهُمْ لَا يَسْتَكْبِرُوْنَ۩‏(15)\n\nOnly those believe in Our signs who, when they are reminded of them, fall down in prostration and celebrate the praise of their Lord, and they are not arrogant.\nتَتَجَافٰى جُنُوْبُهُمْ عَنِ الْمَضَاجِعِ يَدْعُوْنَ رَبَّهُمْ خَوْفًا وَّطَمَعًا وَّمِمَّا رَزَقْنٰهُمْ يُنْفِقُوْنَ‏(16)\n\nTheir sides vacate their beds to supplicate their Lord in fear and hope, and they spend out of what We have provided them.\nفَلَا تَعْلَمُ نَفْسٌ مَّاۤ اُخْفِىَ لَهُمْ مِّنْ قُرَّةِ اَعْيُنٍ‌ۚ جَزَآءًۢ بِمَا كَانُوْا يَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(17)\n\nNo one knows what delights have been kept hidden for them [in the Hereafter] as a reward for what they used to do.\nاَفَمَنْ كَانَ مُؤْمِنًا كَمَنْ كَانَ فَاسِقًا‌ ؕ لَا يَسْتَوٗنَ‏(18)\n\nIs someone who is faithful like someone who is a transgressor? They are not equal.\nاَمَّا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَعَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِ فَلَهُمْ جَنّٰتُ الْمَاْوٰى نُزُلًاۢ بِمَا كَانُوْا يَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(19)\n\nAs for those who have faith and do righteous deeds, for them will be the gardens of the Abode—a hospitality for what they used to do.\nوَاَمَّا الَّذِيْنَ فَسَقُوْا فَمَاْوٰٮهُمُ النَّارُ‌ؕ كُلَّمَاۤ اَرَادُوْۤا اَنْ يَّخْرُجُوْا مِنْهَاۤ اُعِيْدُوْا فِيْهَا وَ قِيْلَ لَهُمْ ذُوْقُوْا عَذَابَ النَّارِ الَّذِىْ كُنْتُمْ بِهٖ تُكَذِّبُوْنَ‏(20)\n\nAs for those who have transgressed, their refuge will be the Fire. Whenever they seek to leave it, they will be turned back into it and told: ‘Taste the punishment of the Fire which you used to deny.’\nوَلَنُذِيْقَنَّهُمْ مِّنَ الْعَذَابِ الْاَدْنٰى دُوْنَ الْعَذَابِ الْاَكْبَرِ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَرْجِعُوْنَ‏(21)\n\nWe shall surely make them taste the nearer punishment prior to the greater punishment, so that they may come back.\nوَمَنْ اَظْلَمُ مِمَّنْ ذُكِّرَ بِاٰيٰتِ رَبِّهٖ ثُمَّ اَعْرَضَ عَنْهَا‌ؕ اِنَّا مِنَ الْمُجْرِمِيْنَ مُنْتَقِمُوْنَ‏(22)\n\nWho is a greater wrongdoer than him who is reminded of his Lord’s signs, whereat he disregards them? Indeed, We shall take vengeance upon the guilty.\nوَلَقَدْ اٰتَيْنَا مُوْسَى الْكِتٰبَ فَلَا تَكُنْ فِىْ مِرْيَةٍ مِّنْ لِّقَآئِهٖ‌ وَجَعَلْنٰهُ هُدًى لِّبَنِىْۤ اِسْرَآءِيْلَۚ‏(23)\n\nCertainly We gave Moses the Book, [declaring], ‘Do not be in doubt about the encounter with Him,’ and We made it a [source of] guidance for the Children of Israel.\nوَ جَعَلْنَا مِنْهُمْ اَئِمَّةً يَّهْدُوْنَ بِاَمْرِنَا لَمَّا صَبَرُوْا‌ ؕ وَ كَانُوْا بِاٰيٰتِنَا يُوْقِنُوْنَ‏(24)\n\nWhen they had been patient and had conviction in Our signs, We appointed amongst them imams to guide [the people] by Our command.\nاِنَّ رَبَّكَ هُوَ يَفْصِلُ بَيْنَهُمْ يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ فِيْمَا كَانُوْا فِيْهِ يَخْتَلِفُوْنَ‏(25)\n\nIndeed your Lord will judge between them on the Day of Resurrection concerning that about which they used to differ.\nاَوَلَمْ يَهْدِ لَهُمْ كَمْ اَهْلَكْنَا مِنْ قَبْلِهِمْ مِّنَ الْقُرُوْنِ يَمْشُوْنَ فِىْ مَسٰكِنِهِمْ‌ ؕ اِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ لَاٰيٰتٍ ؕ اَفَلَا يَسْمَعُوْنَ‏(26)\n\nDoes it not dawn upon them how many generations We have destroyed before them, amid [the ruins of] whose dwellings they walk? There are indeed signs in that. Will they not then listen?\nاَوَلَمْ يَرَوْا اَنَّا نَسُوْقُ الْمَآءَ اِلَى الْاَرْضِ الْجُرُزِ فَنُخْرِجُ بِهٖ زَرْعًا تَاْكُلُ مِنْهُ اَنْعَامُهُمْ وَاَنْفُسُهُمْ‌ؕ اَفَلَا يُبْصِرُوْنَ‏(27)\n\nDo they not see that We carry water to the parched earth and with it We bring forth crops, from which they eat, themselves and their cattle? Will they not then see?\nوَيَقُوْلُوْنَ مَتٰى هٰذَا الْفَتْحُ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ صٰدِقِيْنَ‏(28)\n\nThey say, ‘When will this judgement be, if you are truthful?’\nقُلْ يَوْمَ الْفَتْحِ لَا يَنْفَعُ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْۤا اِيْمَانُهُمْ وَلَا هُمْ يُنْظَرُوْنَ‏(29)\n\nSay, ‘On the day of judgement their [newly found] faith will not avail the faithless, nor will they be granted any respite.’\nفَاَعْرِضْ عَنْهُمْ وَانْتَظِرْ اِنَّهُمْ مُّنْتَظِرُوْنَ‏(30)\n\nSo turn away from them, and wait. They too are waiting.",
  "merits": "Surah al-Sajdah (The Adoration)\nThere are 30 verses in this Surah and it was revealed in Makkah. Some scholars say that the 19th, 20th and 21st verses of this Surah are ‘Madani’. In the commentary of Burhan it is narrated from the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) that the reward for reciting Surah al-Sajdah and [Surah al-Mulk](A71) is the same as what reward is gotten if one spends the entire night of Qadr in worship. It is said that the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) used to recite these Surahs before sleeping.\nThe person who recites this Surah will be given 60 rewards, forgiven 60 sins and raised 60 levels nearer to Allah (s.w.t.). Imam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) has said that one who recites this Surah will be given his book of deeds in his right hand on the Day of Judgement and will be counted from among the friends of the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) and his family. Keeping this Surah in writing works as a cure from aches and pains."
}
